# --- agent runtime state (never commit; config.json gets node_token after 1st run) ---
agent/model_slice*/
agent/*.log
agent/config.test.json
agent/config.bad.json
# every local agent config, not just the test ones -- config.driver.json holds this machine's
# node_token and relay ticket. `agent/config.node-*.json` below did not match config.driver.json.
agent/config.*.json
# ...and the BASE name too, which `agent/config.*.json` never matched. It was tracked, holding a
# null template, on a path that on every real installation holds a live `node_token` -- the one
# credential for that node's earnings ([P39]: lose the token, lose the money). Two ways that
# ends badly: an operator commits after their agent has run and publishes their own token to a
# public repo, and `git checkout` on a node replaces a working config with nulls and detaches it
# from its balance. `ensure_config()` writes DEFAULT_CONFIG when the file is absent, so a fresh
# clone still starts cleanly -- nothing needed the template to be committed.
agent/config.json
# the atomic _save() keeps the previous config alongside the new one, node_token included
agent/*.prev
# holds a wallet private_key. The `*.key` rule further down does NOT match a .json filename,
# and this repo is public.
agent/payout_key.json

# --- moderation log (driver-local, holds prompt snippets -- never commit) ---
safety/*.log
ui/*.log

# --- coordinator runtime state / secrets (never commit) ---
# SQLite DB holds real node auth tokens — must never be pushed
*.db
*.db-wal
*.db-shm
coordinator/node_tokens.json
coordinator/nodes.local.json
# prune_test_accounts.py's audit trail — holds per-account balances, same privacy class as
# the DB itself (Session 25: no node's earnings are public).
coordinator/prune_log.json
coordinator/reconcile_log.json

# --- private / pre-public docs (keep out of the public repo) ---
TOKENOMICS.md
# Unpublished research. Stays local until submission; publishing here first would be our
# own prior art against us. Naming the contents in this file would defeat the purpose.
research/
# Internal planning and strategy, untracked in Session 42. These hold the Oracle VM's IP, home
# LAN addresses, founder-allocation and legal/budget notes — nothing that is a credential, but
# none of it is the public story either. Untracking only stops future commits: every one of
# them is still readable in this repo's history.
NEURON_COMPLETE_PROJECT.md
FIRST_STRANGER.md
PETALS_NOTES.md
distributed-ai-network-plan.html
# Outreach targets and approach notes. Unlike the four above, this one was never committed on
# any branch, so ignoring it is genuinely sufficient — there is no history to walk back.
OUTREACH.md
# Growth tooling spec (broadcast / opt-in list / scout). Same class as OUTREACH.md: audience
# targeting, channel strategy and the legal reasoning behind the non-goals — none of it is the
# public story, and it names the operator's jurisdiction. Never committed on any branch.
GROWTH_PLAN.md

# --- blockchain work-in-progress (NRN ERC-20, migration, deploy) ---
# Nothing here is deployed and nothing here is public yet. Holds a deploy key path,
# wallet addresses and the ledger snapshot it migrates — keep it local until launch.
blockchain/
# ...and the npm toolchain it needs. node_modules must sit above blockchain/ so that
# `sources: "."` in hardhat.config.js does not treat OpenZeppelin as project sources.
/node_modules/
/package.json
/package-lock.json

